preConditionHook:
// A run counted back from the current bar reaches minBars exactly when none of
// the first minBars pairs broke it, so the counter is written as that bounded
// all-pairs test -- same firing bars, no persisted state, and the EL twin is
// the same loop statement for statement.
// The breaking test is STRICT (an equal low keeps a bull micro channel alive,
// Brooks's "no bar with a lower low"), and it is an ordinary EL relational, so
// el_lt/el_gt carry the measured 2.22e-12 tolerance.
//
// minTicks (added 2026-09-17, tick-unit list) IS HOW DEEP A PULLBACK HAS TO BE
// TO BREAK THE RUN: a bar breaks the bull channel only if its low is at least
// minTicks below the prior bar's low, so a pullback of up to minTicks - 1 ticks
// is forgiven. AT THE DEFAULT minTicks = 1 the subtracted term is
// (1 - 1) * tickSize = 0 and the test is character for character the original
// strict one -- existing behaviour and every existing template are unchanged --
// and it is simultaneously the merged T02 key HigherLowStreak at ITS default,
// whose alive-condition is low[i] >= low[i + 1] - (minTicks - 1) * tickSize
// with noPullbackBars = minBars. The two requirements coincide exactly, so
// nothing had to be traded off. Sources for the tolerance: R00-55 (no pullback
// bar within the last 5 bars, a pullback bar being a low below the prior low by
// at least minTicks) and V09-02 (the strict single-bar form).
//
// EL: the same comparison, low[kk] < low[kk + 1] - (minTicks - 1) * tickSize,
// clearing chanLow.
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local; every scratch value is a localVariables entry,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
chanLow = true;
chanHigh = true;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)minBars; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], low[i + 1] - (minTicks - 1) * tickSize)) chanLow = false;
    if (el_gt(high[i], high[i + 1] + (minTicks - 1) * tickSize)) chanHigh = false;
}
